    /// <summary>
    /// The eruptions of Arieki's geysers and hornitos: one world_usable row (PlacedUsables, a
    /// RANDOMEXPLOSION) at each vent the client's maps draw, rows 10001-10308.
    ///
    /// The vents are scenery in the .maps - TerraAriekiPlainsGeyser* on Torden Plains, and
    /// TerraAriekiGenHornito* and TerraAriekiLigoHornito* on Burning Steps, Magma Caverns, the
    /// three Torden maps and the Fluxite Mines - with no state and no use. What erupts is a
    /// separate object no .map places, which the live servers put down: RandomExplosionAriekiGeyser
    /// (8090, "Geyser Blast") and RandomExplosionAriekiHornitoEruption (9353, "Hornito Eruption"),
    /// on the particle proxies' empty mesh, whose one state's effect is the build-up and whose
    /// blast is OBJ_DAMAGE 6 or 7. Each row stands at its vent's position in the .map, which is
    /// the vent's base; the vent's .map entity id and class are in its comment. The smoking
    /// hornitos (TerraAriekiLigoHornitoSmoking*) and the small geysers
    /// (TerraAriekiPlainsGeyserSmall*) are left out: 34 and 22 of them, that stay scenery.
    ///
    /// The blast is the client's for both arguments: 50-100 within 6 m (actiondata OBJ_DAMAGE 6
    /// and 7). How often a vent goes off is ours: each has a shortest wait of 30-60 s and a
    /// longest 15-45 s more, drawn once per vent (seeded by its entity id, so the rows are the
    /// same each time they are made), and every wait between two blasts is a fresh roll between
    /// the two. So no two vents keep the same time.
    /// </summary>
